iffusion process model with unknown drift and variable-independent diffusivity, we construct a composite methodology to perform Bayesian inference for the coefficients. Recent development of non-parametric Bayesian estimation of the drift has been restricted to dimension one, since the local time process is unavailable in the multi-dimensional case. We involve the empirical measure instead and show that the drift likelihood has a quadratic form, which allows a conjugate Gaussian measure prior whose precision operator is chosen to be a high order differential operator. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nConsistent nonparametric Bayesian inference for discretely observed scalar diffusions - Research portal Eindhoven University of Technology (https://research.tue.nl/en/publications/consistent-nonparametric-bayesian-inference-for-discretely-observ/)\nciteturn961search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # Consistent nonparametric Bayesian inference for discretely observed scalar diffusions ... Research output: Contribution to journal › Article › Academic › peer-review ... We study Bayes procedures for the problem of nonparametric drift estimation for one-dimensional, ergodic diffusion models from discrete-time, low-frequency data. ... Keywords: Bayesian nonparametrics; drift function; posterior consistency; posterior distribution; stochastic differential equations; wavelets ... abstract = \"We study Bayes procedures for the problem of nonparametric drift estimation for one-dimensional, ergodic diffusion models from discrete-time, low-frequency data.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReversible jump MCMC for nonparametric drift estimation for diffusion processes - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S016794731300090X)\nciteturn961search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; In the context of nonparametric Bayesian estimation a Markov ch